footage from a cancelled star wars game  is out in the wild february's xbox games  with gold have been revealed and  hyperscape is dying  new footage of the cancelled star wars  1313 has been unearthed by the vault and  it shows off gameplay of the franchise's  iconic bounty hunter boba fett as he  explores several locations while some of  the video shows off the game in an early  stage of production it's still a  fascinating look at some gameplay  elements including exploration of a bar  chasing down targets and establishing  fed's reputation as a no-nonsense gun  for hire star wars 1313 was originally  revealed at e3 2012 and would have seen  players descend into the criminal  underworld of the galactic empire's  capital city coruscant a year later the  project was officially dead after disney  acquired the star wars franchise and put  all ongoing projects on hiatus the  location of the game level 1313  eventually made its way into several  episodes of star wars the clone wars  interestingly fett was reportedly not  meant to be the star of the game as  author jason schreier noted in his book  blood sweat and pixels lucas arts  leadership was instructed by star wars  creator george lucas to replace the  original protagonist with a pre-empire  version of fed this came well into the  development of 1313 after lucasarts had  cast actor wilson bethel established a  backstory for his character and had  spent significant time on his technical  development i have to admit i'm really  impressed by this gameplay especially  considering it's around a decade old it  it looks modern in many ways and reminds  me of uncharted in so many ways and when  you take into consideration that  uncharted writer amy hennig was also a  part of this project  we could have totally had uncharted in  space uncharted mixed with star wars is  there a way i can fund this project so  that like another studio could pick it  up and continue making it just for me  i'm sorry you you can't play it maybe if  you come over my house you could you  could play for like two minutes and then  just watch me play  moving on to free games xbox has  revealed the next batch of free games  for xbox live gold and game pass  ultimate subscribers february's games  with gold lineup includes two xbox one  games and a pair of 360 games that are  backwards compatible there's probably a  good chance you haven't heard of these  games but here they are broken sword 5  the serpent's curse aerial knights never  yield hydrophobia and band of bugs a  runner like ariel knight seems perfect  for my phone a backbone and remote play  so i'm excited to get into that let me  know what you're excited for in the  comments  in other news ubisoft has announced that  it will be shutting down the servers and  ending development on hyperscape it's  free to play battle royale game on april  28th in a statement the company said  quote we set out to create a vertical  close quarters and fast-paced shooter  experience and we're extremely grateful  to our community for joining us on our  journey we will be taking key learnings  from this game into future products  hyperscape launched in august 2020 and  the game's third and final season was  released in march 2021 but the game  hasn't had any substantial updates since  then it also struggled to find an  audience on twitch despite being closely  integrated with the platform viewers  could interact with the game such as  being able to vote on where a match  takes place or what kinds of modifiers  would be turned on  ubisoft concluded their message by  saying quote to the hyperescape  community thank you for your passion and  dedication to the world of neo arcadia  both inside and outside of the game your  devotion to the game we built will  always be cherished to say i was  horrible at hyperscape is a complete  understatement but let me know if you're  going to miss it in the comments and  what you plan on playing instead there's  plenty of battle royales out 